"""Scoped, measured material/reference and Vulkan-query milestones."""
def apply(sections,sources,source,section,table,cite):
 for sid,title,path,note in [
  ('S86','Basix Vulkan feature/property query','vulkan-capabilities.json','Physical-device queries for16 candidates; no logical device, advanced shader, CLAS build or performance result. RTX4090/NVIDIA617.42; validation clean apart from19 explicitly counted loader environment warnings.'),
  ('S87','Basix material conformance','material-results.json','70 CPU correctness checks and2048 GPU evaluation/PDF cases. No-op shader fails8192 sentinels; final working run passes with zero validation warnings/errors. No GPU sampling or textured-material acceptance.'),
  ('S88','Basix CPU reference PT','reference-results.json','61 analytic/transport/determinism/boundary checks plus actual256x256/64SPP original scene. CPU progressive NEE/MIS/RR; no GPU PT, import, textures or motion guides.')]:
  source(sid,title,'https://github.com/BasixMaster/Basix_Engine/blob/main/docs/'+path,note,kind='local measured correctness',rights='Original Basix code and selected receipts MIT; no vendor runtime included.')
 by={s['id']:s for s in sections}
 by['vulkan-features']['body']+='''<h3>Actual query receipt · not execution</h3><p>The named local RTX4090 driver reports the NV cluster feature, all seven matrix2 feature bits, cooperative-vector inference/training, partitioned AS and EXT invocation reorder. Linear swept spheres are not advertised. The probe records numeric limits and all NV/NVX extension names; matrix/vector type-dimension tuple enumeration remains a next step.</p><p>No logical device is created by this probe, so its enabled/oracle/performance fields remain false. Validation has zero unreviewed warnings/errors;19 loader messages concern existing Galaxy layer names and layers explicitly disabled by the process filter. They are counted separately through a narrow message-ID/text allowlist. <a href="vulkan-capabilities.json">Capability query receipt</a>.</p>'''+cite('S86')
 section('reference-renderer','Reference renderer: first measured material and transport slice','''
<p><strong>M2 is partial.</strong> Shared material evaluation and a CPU transport oracle now exist. GPU progressive PT, scene import, textures and temporal guides remain pending. Basix remains Vulkan-first through NoGraphicsAPI; the CPU renderer is the independent reference for that future GPU path.</p>
<figure><img src="assets/reference-cornell.png" width="256" height="256" alt="Original CPU path-traced box scene with diffuse walls and diffuse and rough-metal spheres"><figcaption>Actual CPU output:256×256,64SPP,seed20261028,depth8; Reinhard plus sRGB preview. An original analytic test scene, not a UE-detail or real-time performance demonstration.</figcaption></figure>
<h3>Material contract</h3><p>Original MIT Lambert and single-scatter isotropic GGX use stable material IDs and a shared evaluation/PDF/sampling contract. CPU tests cover analytic Lambert values, reciprocity, energy quadrature, mixture-PDF histograms and explicit null samples. The metallic/roughness diffuse attenuation is a conservative approximation, not exact glTF or multiple-scattering compensation.</p>
<p>The GPU probe checks2,048 uploaded float cases against CPU double evaluation:8,192 finite/nonnegative BRDF/PDF components within0.0003+0.001×|reference|. Minimum roughness and grazing cases include very large BRDF values; maximum absolute error alone is misleading. Maximum error/tolerance is0.000591046. An isolated no-op shader fails every sentinel check. Full GPU process logs contain zero validation warnings/errors. GPU sampling is not yet tested.</p>
<h3>Transport contract</h3><p>The CPU renderer traces analytic spheres/triangles with one-sided triangle emitters, area-light next-event estimation, power-heuristic MIS and compensated Russian roulette. Maximum depth explicitly truncates transport. Immutable scenes validate finite values and unique IDs. Counter-keyed samples preserve batch identity; stable IDs control equal-hit and light ordering.</p>
<p>61 checks include analytic intersections, rectangular-light irradiance, independent convergence and NEE/MIS/RR agreement, constant-environment Lambert energy, deterministic batching and invalid input rejection. The actual published preview has196,608 finite nonnegative linear components. Its elapsed CPU time is a local oracle cost, not a GPU benchmark.</p>
<p><strong>Next gate:</strong> implement GPU material sampling and a small Vulkan ray-query progressive integrator against this reference, then import and depth/motion conventions. Existing device-loss and dynamic DLSS recovery gates remain open.</p>
<p><a href="material-results.json">Material receipt</a> · <a href="reference-results.json">Reference receipt</a> · <a href="https://github.com/BasixMaster/Basix_Engine/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION.md">Reproduce the targets</a></p>'''+cite('S87','S88'))
 by['summary']['body']+='<p><strong>Measured implementation:</strong> material conformance and a CPU reference PT now pass their scoped checks. M2 remains partial while GPU PT/import/motion are pending.</p>'+cite('S87','S88')
 by['lessons']['body']+='<p><strong>Reference before optimization:</strong> compare native extension paths against ordinary rays and scalar/material oracles. Shader no-op controls detect untouched output even with successful API calls. Feature queries establish a candidate path; they do not establish execution or speed.</p>'+cite('S86','S87','S88')

def enrich_library(library):
 library['summary'].append('M2 partial: tested material CPU/GPU evaluation and CPU progressive reference; Vulkan advanced feature queries recorded separately from execution.')
 library['findings'].append(dict(id='F18',title='Reference material and CPU transport gates pass within narrow scopes',question_ids=['Q2'],topic='rendering',claim='GPU material evaluation/PDF matches a tested CPU model, and CPU transport passes analytic/convergence checks. Advanced Vulkan features have query evidence only.',evidence_type='measured',confidence='high',context='2026-10-28 local Windows RTX4090/NVIDIA617.42; pinned headers/compiler and validation.',strengths='Independent analytic CPU checks, poisoned GPU outputs/no-op negative control, deterministic batch and actual image checks.',limitations='No GPU sampling/PT, importer, textures, motion guides, advanced-extension execution or performance comparison.',implications='Keep M2 partial and optional CLAS/neural execution pending; port the reference to Vulkan before optimizing.',tags=['materials','reference PT','Vulkan','roadmap'],evidence=[dict(source_id=s,locator='Receipt scope and numeric results',relation='supports',note='Scoped local acceptance only.') for s in ['S86','S87','S88']]))
 library['scope_changes'].append('Implemented original material oracle and CPU progressive PT; recorded Vulkan feature/property queries without promoting advanced extension execution.')
